  "note": "Election of the Newry Urban District Council, nominations taken 5 January 1932 (Newry Telegraph, 7 January 1932, p. 5). No ward was contested. Four valid nominations (Bannon, Cunningham, Murphy, Ruddy); McAnulty withdrew and the papers of Mackin and Neary were invalid. Michael Griffin and Peter McGeough were deemed re-elected on their 1929 votes. Griffin had also been validly nominated in the West Ward and had to choose between them; if he sat for West the South seat became a casual vacancy to be filled by co-option (Mackin or Neary were expected). Recorded here as not filled at the return. Returned unopposed."
